From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: misc-de <misc-de@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] location-manager: Remember the location answers of native
 apps

Plinius: a native app asking geoclue for the location (AuthorizeApp)
was asked "Yes" or "No" on every start, nothing was remembered (two
TODOs). It now gets the same three buttons as every other access
question, and the answer is kept in the permission store the way
xdg-desktop-portal 1.22 (location.c) keeps it for Flatpak apps: table
"location", id "location", the app's entry [accuracy, last use], the
accuracy one of NONE, COUNTRY, CITY, NEIGHBORHOOD, STREET, EXACT and the
last use g_get_monotonic_time() as there. The key is the desktop id
geoclue names, the same key GNOME Settings' Location page lists and
switches between EXACT and NONE.

- entry NONE (or an unknown accuracy, as in xdg-desktop-portal): denied
  without asking
- entry at the level asked for or a finer one: allowed without asking
- otherwise (no entry, a coarser one, a malformed one) asked; "Always
  Allow" stores the level asked for, "Don't Allow" NONE, "Allow Once"
  and a dialog swiped away store nothing
- no permission store (or no answer within 2 s): asked as before, and
  nothing stored

The maximum level and the global switch come first, as before.
location-permission.c holds the lookup, the decision and the write.
